  "description": "Reid Bikes H20 | 20 inch kids' bike\nThe perfect 20\" pedal bike for 6-9 year olds, to help improve control and confidence.\nLightweight performance meets kid-sized versatility – the ideal 20\" kids' bike for growing riders. At just 7.6kg, this Reid Bikes 20\" bike offers an impressively light frame that makes riding easier, faster, and more fun for kids ready to explore new terrain. The low weight helps improve control and confidence, giving young riders the edge they need to keep pushing their limits.\nPart of the Reid Bikes H Series kids' bike range, this H20 kids' bike is built from strong yet lightweight 6061 aluminium alloy, the frame and fork provide durability without unnecessary bulk. The 7-speed Shimano drivetrain with smooth shifters and a 14-28T cassette lets kids tackle hills and varying terrain with ease and confidence.\nReliable Jak V-brakes and alloy brake levers are sized for smaller hands, while the 20 x 1.5\" Vee tires offer traction and stability on a variety of surfaces. The comfortable junior saddle, alloy riser bars, and ergonomic grips are designed to keep kids riding longer and feeling great.\nPerfect for confident kids stepping up their riding game, this lightweight bike combines performance, comfort, and simplicity in a package that grows with every adventure.\nWho is the Reid Bikes H20 for?\nThe H20 kids' bike is ideal for:\n\n6–9 year olds ready to take their riding further\n\nYoung riders developing greater control and confidence on two wheels\n\nChildren moving up from a 16\" kids' bike and ready for a bigger bike\n\nRiders exploring different terrain, from parks and bike paths to local trails\n\nKids ready to learn how to use gears and tackle hills and changing terrain\n\nGrowing riders who want a lightweight, versatile bike for everyday adventures\n\nParents looking for a durable, easy-to-handle bike that can keep up with more adventurous riding\n\nFind the right fit\nChoosing the right bike size helps your child ride comfortably, confidently and safely. Use our Kids' Bike Size Guide by clicking the tab above to find the right Reid bike based on your child’s height and age.",
